# CI/CD workflows land here in Level 3.
#
# This project already has everything CI will need to run:
#   npm run compact    — compile the Compact contract
#   npm run test       — run the test suite
#   npm run typecheck  — typecheck the TypeScript glue
#
# Note for whoever wires this up: the Compact toolchain is NOT an npm package.
# CI must install the devtools first and pin the version in .compact-version:
#
#   curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -LsSf \
#     https://github.com/midnightntwrk/compact/releases/latest/download/compact-installer.sh | sh
#   source $HOME/.local/bin/env
#   compact update "$(cat .compact-version)"
#
# See the Troubleshooting section of the README for the toolchain/runtime
# version-lock that makes pinning mandatory.
